b. Create visualizations (histograms, box plots) to depict the distribution of a
variable and analyze its characteristics.
CODE:
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns
plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))
plt.hist(sales, bins=10, color="skyblue", edgecolor="black")
plt.title("Histogram of Sales")
plt.xlabel("Sales")
plt.ylabel("Frequency")
plt.show()
OUTPUT:

CODE:
plt.figure(figsize=(8,3))
sns.boxplot(x=sales, color="orange")
plt.title("Box Plot of Sales")
plt.xlabel("Sales")
plt.show()
